\section{Conclusion}\label{sec:conclusion}
This study presented an approach to forecasting spectrum demand using AI techniques. The methodology integrated data from site licenses and crowdsourced sources, validated against real-world mobile network traffic data. An enhanced proxy was proposed that achieved an R$^2$ value of 0.89, indicating strong predictive accuracy. The ML models were tested and validated across five major Canadian cities, demonstrating their generalizability and robustness. As a result, this framework supports dynamic spectrum planning, enabling efficient and responsive resource allocation and policy adjustments to meet evolving network demands.


